{
  "rationale": "Use a small sensor plant plus a motion-command plant, then layer compact specifications that map sensed obstacle conditions to exactly one safe recovery action. Forward motion is the default in clear space, random_walk is used only as a mild coverage bias after successful forward pulses, obstacle states always pass through recovery first, move_backward is restricted to front-obstacle escape, and full_rotate is only reachable through a dedicated last-resort stuck path after repeated front blockage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and actuation into plant automata and encode policy in specifications.",
    "Bias toward move_forward in clear space, allow occasional random_walk only in clear/search mode, and use short directed turns as default recovery.",
    "Make action states one-shot on their primary controllable and total on uncontrollable events, with path_clear usually self-looping in commit states.",
    "Restrict move_backward to dedicated front-obstacle recovery and restrict full_rotate to a dedicated stuck/last_resort chain only."
  ],
